<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Tool> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An element of hardware and/or software utilized to carry out a particular function."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvaluationResultType/fail> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Indicates a failed evaluation where the requirement or condition is not met."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/verificationPostcondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Verification postcondition are explicit criteria, states, or conditions that are true immediately after a verification method (such as a test, inspection, or analysis) has been performed, confirming the successful execution and complete outcomes of the verification."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/MeasureOfLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The measure of length refers to the dimension of an object or space that describes how long it is, typically expressed in various units depending on the system of measurement being used."@en .
