<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "International Business Identifier (IBID) <https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/> is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the ISO/DIS 25500-3 <https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html> draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (|) (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/secureSoftwareAttestation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A reference to information assuring that the software is developed using security practices as defined by NIST SP 800-218 Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1 <https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final> or CISA Secure Software Development Attestation Form <https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-software-development-attestation-form>."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/modifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "modifiedBy"@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Bundle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A bundle is a collection of Elements that have a shared context."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/LifecycleScopeType/other> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A relationship has other specific context information necessary to capture that the above set of enumerations does not handle."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/cve> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core> .
